@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+## Why
+
+A task is only identified by its title, so anything that refers to a task stops working once the task is renamed. The app needs a stable reference.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Every task gets a unique string `id`, assigned by the list when the task is added and never changed afterwards (renaming, completing, tagging keep it).
+- The list gets `get(id)`, returning `Result<Task>`; an unknown id fails with `not-found`.
+- `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove` accept either a task's id or its title.
+- Ids are never reused, even after a task is removed.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-ids`: stable unique task identifiers, lookup by id, and id-or-title addressing of tasks.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None (`openspec/specs/` is empty).
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/domain/task.ts`: `Task` gains `readonly id: string`; `createTask` receives the id from its caller.
+- `src/domain/list.ts`: id assignment, `get`, id-or-title resolution.
+- `src/index.ts`: no new export is needed (`Task` and `TaskList` are already exported and carry the new field and method). **The public API changes**: `Task.id` and `TaskList.get`.
+- Tests in `test/list.test.ts`; existing tests comparing whole tasks must include `id`.
+- Project rules: no new dependency; the domain stays free of clock and randomness (ids come from a counter held by the list, not from random values); `get` returns a `Result` and nothing throws; new exported functions keep their TSDoc.
